    "knockdown_precision": 0.9,
    "knockdown_conservative_reference": 0.1407,
    "geometry_rule": "On the 5 percent mass ceiling, face thickness is the value that maximises the lesser of the five mode safety factors at knockdown 0.20. Global buckling in that lesser factor is the NASA CR-1457 handbook value, gamma_d times Kc, not the classical pressure stacked on top of it. The 0.90 column is the same geometry with the classical pressure scaled to 0.90. The handbook does not authorise gamma_d of 0.90."
